{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933431-alien-in-the-world-of-darkness-question","id":933431,"title":"Alien in the world of darkness question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-18T08:33:51-07:00","id":933431,"title":"Alien in the world of darkness question","content":"i recall reading somewhere that aliens have some kind of imperfection like a weakness to....<br /> <br /> \u200bNow out of curiosity what kind of weakness would the Doctor have? in Doctor Who he seems to withstand physical wounds, extreme temperatures, and radiation much better than humans, as far as i can tell the beings of Gallifrey don't seem yo have a weakness except maybe pride if that could even be considered one? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T11:55:48-07:00","id":933510,"title":"","content":"Needs to have the last word. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, you're right -- the Doctor doesn't have physical/supernatural weaknesses. But you can generally speaking model him as a human with a few contextual benefits. I wrote up the Fourth Doctor as a starting character once, which is a stretch but not a huge one.<br /> <br /> (He is <i>technically</i> allergic to &quot;certain gases in the Praxis range,&quot; but that's pretty obscure.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fHeSbtsGCmqLjLU5CsbPVBp0qXQVz_UDKlgE8XZuwqY/edit